<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.dailybriefing</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py</string>
        <string>--daily-briefing</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Runs once a day at 7:00am, ahead of com.curant.proactive.plist's
         8:00am slot -- these are two separate, deliberately different
         jobs (see run_daily_briefing's docstring in curant-watcher.py for
         why this isn't just a duplicate of the proactive-check job). -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>7</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-dailybriefing.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-dailybriefing-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp com.curant.dailybriefing.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.dailybriefing.plist

This is Grace-exclusive, gated in curant-cli's daily_briefing() function
(checks get_customer_august_tier(config) == "grace") -- loading this job
on a non-Grace customer's Mac is harmless, it just always results in
should_send=false, same "safe to always run" pattern as
com.curant.proactive.plist.

To test immediately rather than waiting for 7am, run curant-watcher.py
with the --daily-briefing flag directly (see ProgramArguments above).

Logs land at /tmp/curant-dailybriefing.log and /tmp/curant-dailybriefing-error.log.
-->
